        "tab_color": "#eae1d5",
        "margin_top": 68,
        "margin_bottom": 68,
        "title": "USDA Organic Integrity",
        "max_width": 73,
        "content": "<p>Several Hemplucid products carry <a href=\"https://www.usda.gov/farming-and-ranching/organic-farming\">USDA Organic certification</a>—a designation that applies not just to the final extract, but to the entire supply chain. USDA Organic standards govern the soil the hemp is grown in, the cultivation practices used, and the processing methods applied during extraction. This means no synthetic fertilizers, no prohibited pesticides, and no genetically modified organisms at any stage. Our <a href=\"https://hemplucid.com/collections/organic-cbd\">organic CBD collection</a> reflects this commitment.</p><p>Organic certification does not replace third-party testing—it complements it. We test our organic products with the same full-panel protocol described above, because certification verifies process, and testing verifies outcome. You need both.</p>",
        "image": "shopify://shop_images/Group_75.png",
        "image_position": "left"
      }
    },
    "wl_tabbed_image_and_text_EzzGVE": {
      "type": "wl-tabbed-image-and-text",
      "name": "HL Tabbed Image & Text",
      "settings": {
        "cclasses": "",
        "color": "#eae1d5",
        "font_color": "#241f21",
        "link_color": "#C83D1B",
        "show_tab": true,
        "tab_color": "#5a5478",
        "margin_top": 68,
        "margin_bottom": 68,
        "title": "How to Read a Certificate of Analysis",
        "max_width": 73,
        "content": "<p>A COA is a document issued by a third-party laboratory summarizing the test results for a specific product batch. If you’ve never read one before, here are the key terms to look for: </p><p><strong>Analyte:</strong> The substance being measured—for example, CBD, THC, lead, or a specific pesticide. </p><p><strong>LOQ (Limit of Quantification):</strong> The lowest concentration the lab can accurately measure. If a result reads “&lt; LOQ,” it means the substance was either absent or present below the lab’s detection threshold. </p><p><strong>ND (Not Detected):</strong> The substance was not found at any measurable level. This is the result you want to see for contaminants. </p><p><strong>Pass / Fail:</strong> A summary judgment based on whether the measured value falls within acceptable limits. All Hemplucid products must receive a “Pass” on every tested parameter before release. </p><p>If a COA raises questions you can’t resolve on your own, <a href=\"https://hemplucid.com/pages/contact\" title=\"contact our team\">contact our team</a>. We will walk you through it.<br/><br/></p>",
        "image": "shopify://shop_images/lab.png",
        "image_position": "right"
      }
    },
